<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CBR001 Inspections Conducted - Detail, built from legacy's JasperServer report
  (cbr-legacy jasper-server .../CBR001_InspectionReport.rpt_jrxml and its four subreports):
  legacy's sections and coordinates, but for what it got wrong.
  - Each inspection starts a page of its own. Legacy ran on from one inspection to the next, so the
    page that took the last of one and the start of the next carried the first one's header.
  - The PEng's Comment prints only when there is one, its box as tall as it; legacy gave it a page
    of its own, 309 points high, empty or not.
  - The bridge and culvert grids are a band per row, their lines growing with the row, so a long
    value wraps; legacy cut off Crossing Name, the span lengths, Total Length and Site Details.
  - Labels clear of their values and of the grid lines; legacy's crossed a dozen of them.
  - Curb Type is filled; Span Width, which no column holds, is gone; Year Superstructure Installed
    is not printed for a culvert; a hazard not answered prints blank rather than "No"; Repairs and
    Monitors say "None" rather than print an empty table.
  - Report Status names who set the status, and when; legacy named the last editor.
  The span lengths are a field: legacy's span-lengths subreport became a value the service joins.
  The inspection items, repairs and monitoring items are lists on the row, each printed by its
  subreport, compiled once and passed in as P_ITEMS_REPORT, P_REPAIRS_REPORT, P_MONITORS_REPORT.
-->
